{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-7","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-7","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":242,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#prop:dc-ch3-2-7","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-5]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"prop:dc-ch3-2-7","line":695,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[uniform interval of definition]\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch3-2-7}\n\n  \\uses{prop:dc-ch3-2-5, lem:dc-ch3-2-6, lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform, lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow, lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:2.7}\n\n  Given $p\\in M$, there exist a neighborhood $V$ of $p$ in $M$, a number\n  $\\varepsilon>0$, and a $C^\\infty$ map $\\gamma:(-2,2)\\times\\mathcal{U}\\to M$,\n  $\\mathcal{U}=\\{(q,w)\\in TM;\\ q\\in V,\\ w\\in T_qM,\\ |w|<\\varepsilon\\}$, such that\n  $t\\mapsto\\gamma(t,q,w)$, $t\\in(-2,2)$, is the unique geodesic of $M$ passing\n  through $q$ with velocity $w$ at $t=0$, for every $q\\in V$ and $w\\in T_qM$ with\n  $|w|<\\varepsilon$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  The geodesic $\\gamma(t,q,v)$ of \\cref{prop:dc-ch3-2-5} is defined for\n  $|t|<\\delta$ and $|v|<\\varepsilon_1$. By the lemma of homogeneity (2.6),\n  $\\gamma(t,q,\\frac{\\delta v}{2})$ is defined for $|t|<2$. Taking\n  $\\varepsilon<\\frac{\\delta\\varepsilon_1}{2}$, the geodesic $\\gamma(t,q,w)$ is\n  defined for $|t|<2$ and $|w|<\\varepsilon$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[uniform interval of definition] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a64632d6368332d322d37\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23prop%3Adc-ch3-2-5\">↗ prop:dc-ch3-2-5</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-6\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-6</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-7-vuniform\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-7-c1flow\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-7-c2flow\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-5-unique\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:2.7</span></span><p></p>Given <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>, there exist a neighborhood <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V$\">$V$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>, a number <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varepsilon &gt;0$\">$\\varepsilon &gt;0$</span>, and a <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$C^\\infty $\">$C^\\infty $</span> map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :(-2,2)\\times \\mathcal{U}\\to M$\">$\\gamma :(-2,2)\\times \\mathcal{U}\\to M$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathcal{U}=\\{ (q,w)\\in TM;\\  q\\in V,\\  w\\in T_qM,\\  |w|&lt;\\varepsilon \\} $\">$\\mathcal{U}=\\{ (q,w)\\in TM;\\  q\\in V,\\  w\\in T_qM,\\  |w|&lt;\\varepsilon \\} $</span>, such that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\mapsto \\gamma (t,q,w)$\">$t\\mapsto \\gamma (t,q,w)$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\in (-2,2)$\">$t\\in (-2,2)$</span>, is the unique geodesic of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> passing through <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span> with velocity <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w$\">$w$</span> at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t=0$\">$t=0$</span>, for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q\\in V$\">$q\\in V$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w\\in T_qM$\">$w\\in T_qM$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|w|&lt;\\varepsilon $\">$|w|&lt;\\varepsilon $</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch The geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (t,q,v)$\">$\\gamma (t,q,v)$</span> of <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23prop%3Adc-ch3-2-5\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-5\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a64632d6368332d322d35\">subsection 1.1</a> is defined for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|t|&lt;\\delta $\">$|t|&lt;\\delta $</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|v|&lt;\\varepsilon _1$\">$|v|&lt;\\varepsilon _1$</span>. By the lemma of homogeneity (2.6), <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (t,q,\\frac{\\delta v}{2})$\">$\\gamma (t,q,\\frac{\\delta v}{2})$</span> is defined for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|t|&lt;2$\">$|t|&lt;2$</span>. Taking <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varepsilon &lt;\\frac{\\delta \\varepsilon _1}{2}$\">$\\varepsilon &lt;\\frac{\\delta \\varepsilon _1}{2}$</span>, the geodesic <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (t,q,w)$\">$\\gamma (t,q,w)$</span> is defined for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|t|&lt;2$\">$|t|&lt;2$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|w|&lt;\\varepsilon $\">$|w|&lt;\\varepsilon $</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#rem:dc-ch3-2-8","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-5","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-5","label":"prop:dc-ch3-2-5"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#thm:dc-ch3-3-7","title":"thm:dc-ch3-3-7","label":"thm:dc-ch3-3-7"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-7","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-7","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[uniform interval of definition]\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch3-2-7}\n\n  \\uses{prop:dc-ch3-2-5, lem:dc-ch3-2-6, lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform, lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow, lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:2.7}\n\n  Given $p\\in M$, there exist a neighborhood $V$ of $p$ in $M$, a number\n  $\\varepsilon>0$, and a $C^\\infty$ map $\\gamma:(-2,2)\\times\\mathcal{U}\\to M$,\n  $\\mathcal{U}=\\{(q,w)\\in TM;\\ q\\in V,\\ w\\in T_qM,\\ |w|<\\varepsilon\\}$, such that\n  $t\\mapsto\\gamma(t,q,w)$, $t\\in(-2,2)$, is the unique geodesic of $M$ passing\n  through $q$ with velocity $w$ at $t=0$, for every $q\\in V$ and $w\\in T_qM$ with\n  $|w|<\\varepsilon$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  The geodesic $\\gamma(t,q,v)$ of \\cref{prop:dc-ch3-2-5} is defined for\n  $|t|<\\delta$ and $|v|<\\varepsilon_1$. By the lemma of homogeneity (2.6),\n  $\\gamma(t,q,\\frac{\\delta v}{2})$ is defined for $|t|<2$. Taking\n  $\\varepsilon<\\frac{\\delta\\varepsilon_1}{2}$, the geodesic $\\gamma(t,q,w)$ is\n  defined for $|t|<2$ and $|w|<\\varepsilon$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-5","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-5","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-6","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-6","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-vuniform","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c1flow","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-7-c2flow","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-metric-ball","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}